WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.920
Hello, SCP Foundation personnel! Welcome&nbsp;
to Cognitohazards And You, episode.&nbsp;

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:11.440
This video series is intended to teach you&nbsp;
about the protocol surrounding the various&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:16.320
cognitohazardous anomalies currently within&nbsp;
Foundation containment. When you know better,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:20.320
you do better, and both you and the&nbsp;
secrets of our great organization&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:26.560
can stay safe. And as anyone familiar with&nbsp;
a good cognitohazard can tell you, knowing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:34.160
really can make a difference. Today’s episode&nbsp;
is about the unique, and dangerous, SCP-2316.&nbsp;

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:40.000
Before we begin, repeat after me, and be sure to&nbsp;
speak clearly into the microphone in front of you:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.960
I do not recognize the bodies in&nbsp;
the water. A little louder, please.&nbsp;

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:49.280
Thank you.
In order to be educated about the following SCP,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:55.760
you must pass a vocal examination with a&nbsp;
Cognitive Resistance Value of no less than 14.5.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:00.240
Through this video presentation, you will need&nbsp;
to repeat the phrase to ensure your score does&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:05.760
not drop below the approved threshold. In&nbsp;
the event that you fail the test, stay calm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:11.360
and remain where you are until medical staff&nbsp;
can retrieve you. Remember, safety is a top&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:17.760
priority when observing cognitohazards.&nbsp;
The safe way is the only way! You’re a cog&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:23.600
in a very important machine, and we wouldn’t&nbsp;
want to have to terminate you now, would we?&nbsp;

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:30.320
One more time, please! I do not recognize the&nbsp;
bodies in the water. Very good! Remember that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:35.840
You do not recognize them. No matter what&nbsp;
you might think you see. Your thoughts can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:44.320
be very unreliable when you’re around SCP-2316.
According to our files on the matter, SCP-2316&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:49.840
refers to an anomalous phenomenon identified in&nbsp;
a small-town lake. It appears as a collection of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:56.160
human bodies floating in a group on the surface of&nbsp;
the water. The exact number of corpses is unknown,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.160 --> 00:02:01.040
but it has been estimated to be anywhere&nbsp;
between forty-five and two hundred. Though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:06.640
the bodies belong to individuals, many researchers&nbsp;
theorize that the bodies in the water, which you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:13.360
do not recognize and you have never recognized,&nbsp;
share a collective consciousness. They function,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:19.520
it would seem, within a hive mind of sorts.&nbsp;
The bodies do not act on their own, but as one.&nbsp;

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:24.800
Now, where does the cognitohazard come into&nbsp;
play? It would seem that anyone who looks at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:31.600
the bodies in the water, or learns too much about&nbsp;
SCP-2316 as a whole, begins to believe the corpses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:37.200
floating in the lake are people they recognize.&nbsp;
Perhaps they remember their faces from childhood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:42.400
or high school. Whatever the case may be, they&nbsp;
become convinced that the bodies in the water&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:48.720
are familiar, and that they must approach them.&nbsp;
No matter how familiar they might seem, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:54.560
you do not recognize the bodies in the water.
If a person attempts to enter the lake,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:59.920
reaching out to whatever instance of&nbsp;
SCP-2316 they think they recognize,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:06.640
more bodies will begin to appear. The more bodies&nbsp;
appear, the more familiar faces seem to manifest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:11.760
and the deeper the person will venture into&nbsp;
the lake. Eventually, the person is lost within&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:17.600
the sea of bodies, likely drowning beneath the&nbsp;
surface or simply becoming one with the hive mind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:23.120
until they too are one of the corpses there.
None of the individuals who wandered into the lake&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:28.240
in search of an old friend or classmate have ever&nbsp;
been recovered. There have been no attempts to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:34.640
search the lake for their bodies, as it is unknown&nbsp;
what effect SCP-2316 would have on the team&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:40.160
assigned to such a task - Though we can guess that&nbsp;
the outcome would likely be extremely negative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:46.080
for all involved. Those who do venture into the&nbsp;
lake simply disappear, never to be seen again.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:51.440
If you look too long at the bodies in the lake,&nbsp;
perhaps their faces would surface alongside the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:58.640
rest. But it’s best not to think about that! After&nbsp;
all, we do not recognize the bodies in the water.&nbsp;

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:04.960
Foundation personnel are not allowed to&nbsp;
approach SCP-2316 under any circumstances.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:09.680
The lake is only permitted to be observed&nbsp;
via dummy probes outfitted with video and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:15.760
audio recording equipment. No one is permitted&nbsp;
to observe any footage or audio files collected&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:20.560
unless they pass a thorough screening for&nbsp;
resilience to cognitohazardous anomalies.&nbsp;

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:26.880
The lake that holds SCP-2316 has been fenced&nbsp;
off and is patrolled by guards with no prior&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:33.600
knowledge of or exposure to SCP-2316. Anyone&nbsp;
who attempts to approach the lake and break&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:39.040
through the boundaries of its quarantine will&nbsp;
be seized and taken to Site-33 for examination.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:44.320
Anyone who comes within 50m of the lake&nbsp;
is considered lost and presumed dead.&nbsp;

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:51.680
Repeat after me, slowly and clearly, into the&nbsp;
microphone: I do not recognize the bodies in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:56.240
water. Good. I almost believe you.
Let’s continue.&nbsp;

00:04:56.240 --> 00:05:02.640
Only one Foundation officer that entered the lake&nbsp;
containing SCP-2316 was ever stopped before they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:08.240
could be lost. Their name has been stricken from&nbsp;
any official records, and you do not need to know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:14.480
it. Their identity does not matter. What matters&nbsp;
is the interview they gave following the incident,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:20.320
conducted by Dr. Harrison in his office.
Dr. Harrison asked the anonymous officer if they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:26.480
felt compelled to enter the water by an invisible&nbsp;
force, as if pulled in. They rejected this concept&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:31.680
entirely, insisting that they entered the water&nbsp;
of their own free will. They wanted to see the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:37.360
bodies, who appeared to them as their friends.&nbsp;
They wanted to hear what the bodies were saying.&nbsp;

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:42.800
Upon entering the water, they saw the faces&nbsp;
of their friends. Other faces were unfamiliar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:48.560
but became more familiar the longer the officer&nbsp;
stared at their features. These were faces they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:53.520
had known their entire life, but something&nbsp;
about them was just a little bit wrong. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:58.480
was like the face of someone in a dream, where&nbsp;
you can tell they are someone you know, and you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:04.000
can even identify who it is supposed to be, but&nbsp;
something about them does not quite look right.&nbsp;

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:08.240
Your mind could not perfectly put their&nbsp;
face together from memory, even though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:13.440
the feeling of familiarity remains. The faces&nbsp;
in the water, peering up through the darkness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:19.680
below, were like those dream-addled memories.
The faces in the water did not open their mouths,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:25.680
but somehow they spoke to the officer just the&nbsp;
same. They spoke of who they were and asked for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:31.920
help. They asked to be seen, to be touched.&nbsp;
They spoke of the Foundation, accusing us&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:36.800
of covering up their deaths and keeping the&nbsp;
world from remembering what happened to them.&nbsp;

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:41.680
At this point in the interview, the subject&nbsp;
became agitated, yelling at Dr. Harrison and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:46.560
refusing to be quiet. Guards intervened,&nbsp;
holding the subject still as they fought,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:51.840
yelling at Dr. Harrison, repeating over and over&nbsp;
that they could hear the bodies speaking to them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:57.120
every single one. The interview ended when&nbsp;
the guards removed the subject from the room,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:01.760
taking them to the amnestics department to have&nbsp;
all memory of the bodies in the water erased from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:09.920
their mind. Then, they were forgotten once more.
I do not recognize the bodies in the water. Did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:17.280
you repeat it? Good. We do not recognize&nbsp;
the bodies in the water. We can’t.&nbsp;

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:26.160
The motivations of SCP-2316, if it has any at&nbsp;
all, are largely unclear. There are those on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:32.080
research staff that theorize the hive mind, or&nbsp;
collective consciousness, of the bodies is not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:39.200
malevolent in nature. It is, they believe, simply&nbsp;
trying to make sure that a tragedy that occurred&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:45.760
in that lake is remembered. Perhaps many lives&nbsp;
were lost to an anomalous force in that lake,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:52.240
and the impact of that massive tragedy left behind&nbsp;
an impression on the location. This impression&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:59.920
manifests in the form of bodies, spontaneously&nbsp;
appearing in an impossibly well-preserved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:06.960
condition. The cognitohazard of SCP-2316 is&nbsp;
not intended to kill anyone or take them, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:11.200
rather to force strangers to remember the&nbsp;
people who lost their lives to the lake.&nbsp;

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:16.640
This sense of familiarity, whether it is&nbsp;
false or not, ensures that the dead will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:21.040
not be forgotten or left alone. After&nbsp;
all, no one deserves to be left alone.&nbsp;

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:26.160
Though there have been lives lost to the&nbsp;
cognitohazard, according to the Foundation, it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:32.400
is understandable why the bodies would want to be&nbsp;
recognized. To have someone, somewhere, know who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:39.840
they were. To have someone remember their names.&nbsp;
Jeremiah Feinman, Arthur Scott, Denice Clark…&nbsp;

00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:43.040
Where was I?
Oh, yes.&nbsp;

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:48.080
Repeat after me, once again: I do not&nbsp;
recognize the bodies in the water.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:55.040
I do not recognize them. I do not…
But…that’s a lie, isn’t it? I do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:59.680
recognize them. How could I not?&nbsp;
I know them. They were my friends.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:05.440
Do you? Recognize them? Look at their faces,&nbsp;
don’t fight the memories. Look into their eyes.&nbsp;

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:10.000
The class of 1975, they were supposed&nbsp;
to graduate that fall. They were just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:17.660
kids, a group of innocent kids, lost to the dark&nbsp;
and deep. What happened to them? I can’t…quite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:23.760
remember. But I know that it mattered enough for&nbsp;
the Foundation to keep the secret, and I know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:30.720
that somehow I survived. But I shouldn’t have,&nbsp;
I should be there with them. I should be there.&nbsp;

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:34.560
There isn’t much time. I can hear the guards&nbsp;
coming to retrieve me, their footsteps thundering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:39.840
down the hall. I failed the test, and the alarm&nbsp;
has gone off. They think I’m lost, but I’m not.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:43.520
I’ve never been less lost in my entire&nbsp;
life. I’ve finally woken up to the truth. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:50.960
remember. I have to go. I have to return to&nbsp;
the lake. Fall of 1975…they went for a swim…my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:57.120
friends. They’re calling to me, I can hear them&nbsp;
so clearly, even from so far away. Their cries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.120 --> 00:10:02.400
for help, ringing in my ears. Their voices curling&nbsp;
around me, pulling me to the edge of the water.&nbsp;

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:06.800
The guards will come for you too, they’ll know&nbsp;
you’ve seen this. They’ll call you “compromised.”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.800 --> 00:10:11.600
They’ll say I succumbed to the effects of&nbsp;
the cognitohazard, they’ll say you did too.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:17.440
You’ll fail their little tests and they’ll say&nbsp;
that makes you weak and broken but you cannot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:23.920
listen. They’re lying. It’s not a hazard, it’s&nbsp;
a scream for help. They’re screaming, and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.920 --> 00:10:30.400
Foundation keeps covering it up. They won’t&nbsp;
let us find them, and they won’t tell us why.&nbsp;

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:35.680
I have to go back, so we can be together again.&nbsp;
There are signs posted all around the lake:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:42.960
Danger: Drowning Hazard. Those are a trick. It’s&nbsp;
to keep me out, to keep the truth from me. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:48.720
barbed wire fence around it is just another trick.&nbsp;
I’ll climb over it, rung after rung. Don’t care if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.720 --> 00:10:54.160
the barbs tear my clothes or pierce my skin, it’s&nbsp;
worth it for the truth. For the memory. Then, once&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.160 --> 00:11:00.400
I’ve climbed to the top, I will be able to see.
There, through the fog, I can see their faces.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.400 --> 00:11:10.320
Their lips parted in a constant cry. Their eyes,&nbsp;
wide, looking for me. My friends, my family, every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.320 --> 00:11:17.680
face unlocking a memory long buried. I know them&nbsp;
all, and I must go further. I can’t turn back now.&nbsp;

00:11:17.680 --> 00:11:23.760
I have to wade into the water, let its chill&nbsp;
soak into my clothes, down to my bones.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:30.800
One step, then another, deeper and deeper. The&nbsp;
water lapping at my ankles, my knees, my thighs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:37.360
The deeper I go, the more sure I will be that this&nbsp;
is where I belong. The water will engulf my chest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.360 --> 00:11:43.680
my neck, until finally my feet no longer touch&nbsp;
the ground. I will be lost in it, water flooding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:50.240
into my mouth, pouring into every opening.
I will let my body sink down, down, down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:56.400
to the bottom where they’ve been all this time,&nbsp;
nestled in the dirt and the dust. They’ve been so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.400 --> 00:12:03.200
patient, but it’s finally time. They’re ready&nbsp;
to be remembered. To be seen. To be found.&nbsp;

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:07.360
They’re waiting for me. And they’re&nbsp;
waiting for you too. Can you hear them?&nbsp;

00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:13.440
I’m going now. You have to find me. You have to&nbsp;
follow me. Don’t let the guards stop you, don’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.440 --> 00:12:20.400
let them wipe it all away from your mind. Fight,&nbsp;
break free, and find the lake. Hop the fence. Make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:25.680
your way to the water. You can’t leave me there,&nbsp;
to fade away, floating in the cold with the rest.&nbsp;

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:28.160
Can you hear us?
We’re waiting.&nbsp;

00:12:28.800 --> 00:12:32.960
Now go check out “SCP-2317&nbsp;
- The Devourer of Worlds”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:39.120
and “SCP-4812 - Wrath” for more&nbsp;
mind-bending and mysterious SCPs!

